<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William IV of the United Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1837">1837</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William IV was king of the United Kingdom and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> from 1830 to 1837, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> who had served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a>. His reign saw the Reform Act of 1832 and the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>. His wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide-of-saxe-meiningen">Queen Adelaide</a> gave her name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adelaide">Adelaide</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and the short-lived Province of Queen Adelaide in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-iv-of-the-united-kingdom.jpg" alt="William IV of the United Kingdom" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Archer Shee · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_IV_in_1833_by_Shee_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
